<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is a tree, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is a partial configuration on some <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> which maybe empty, and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are two distinct vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distance between <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unique path in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> connecting <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p_{uv})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p_{uv})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of points in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N[p_{uv}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N[p_{uv}]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of neighbors of points in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N[p_{uv}]\setminus V(p_{uv})=\{v_{1},\cdots,v_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N[p_{uv}]\setminus V(p_{uv})=\{v_{1},\cdots,v_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the component of <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\setminus p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\setminus p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for the partition function of the 2-spin system defined on <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> conditioning on <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have (we omit the argument <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> in the second line for simplicity)</span></p>
