<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we are ready to establish SSM for a 2-spin system assuming it satisfies LDC and has a uniform bound on a circle.
We first give the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> be two analytic functions on some complex neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that the Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,\cdots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,\cdots,n</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, suppose that there exists an <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that both <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P(z)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P(z)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(z)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(z)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> on some circle <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for every <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P(z)-Q(z)|\leq\frac{2M}{\rho(r-1)r^{n}},\quad\text{with}\quad r=\dfrac{\rho}{|z-z_{0}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">with</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P(z)-Q(z)|\leq\frac{2M}{\rho(r-1)r^{n}},\quad\text{with}\quad r=\dfrac{\rho}{|z-z_{0}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Cauchy integral formula, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\dfrac{P(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\dfrac{P(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex8Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\dfrac{Q(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\dfrac{Q(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the series <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> on the closed disk <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10 (c.f. Theorem 4.4 in []). ‣ 2.3 Tools from complex analysis ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.
Thus, for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|P(z)-Q(z)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|P(z)-Q(z)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}(a_{k}-b_{k})(z-z_{0})^{k}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}(a_{k}-b_{k})(z-z_{0})^{k}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}\dfrac{|z-z_{0}|^{k}}{2\pi}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\left|\dfrac{P(z)-Q(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}\dfrac{|z-z_{0}|^{k}}{2\pi}\int_{\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})}\left|\dfrac{P(z)-Q(z)}{(z-z_{0})^{k+1}}\mathrm{d}z\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\dfrac{2M}{\rho}\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}r^{-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\dfrac{2M}{\rho}\sum\limits_{k\geq n+1}r^{-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2M}{\rho(r-1)r^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2M}{\rho(r-1)r^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a complex neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the corresponding 2-spin system satisfies LDC and it has a uniform bound on a circle <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then for any <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the 2-spin system exhibits SSM with rate <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\rho/|\lambda|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\rho/|\lambda|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For some arbitrary <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,
some feasible partial configurations <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and some vertex <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the rational functions <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. By LDC, these two functions are analytic and the coefficients of the first <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{G}(v,\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\})</annotation></semantics></math> terms in their Taylor series are equal.
Also, by a uniform bound on the circle <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P(\lambda)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P(\lambda)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(\lambda)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(\lambda)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then the result follows directly from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem17" title="Lemma 17. ‣ 3.2 Local dependence of coefficients and a uniform bound on a circle ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we show that zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients (LDC).
We first introduce a special form of LDC, called point-to-point LDC and we show it implies LDC.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Point-to-point LDC)<span id="Thmtheorem19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system is said to satisfy <em id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">point-to-point LDC</em> (for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) if for
any <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, any feasible configuration <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, and any two vertices <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the functions
<math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,+}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,+}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda):=\frac{Z_{G,v,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}(\lambda)}{Z_{G,u}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and
their corresponding Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}c_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}=c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 20</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a 2-spin system satisfies point-to-point LDC, then it also satisfies LDC.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">When point-to-point LDC holds, we prove LDC by induction of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0,</annotation></semantics></math> the assertion holds immediately. Suppose now that the assertion holds when <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math> then when <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\},</annotation></semantics></math> by point-to-point LDC, the functions
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and
their corresponding Taylor series <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>; similar equality holds for <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall that <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> means the restriction of <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\notin\Lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\notin\Lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> then the two partial configurations are the same. ), and then we have <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence we can apply the induction hypothesis. Then the conclusion follows since <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now, it suffices to prove that point-to-point LDC derives from zero-freeness.
We prove this by establishing a Christoffel-Darboux type identity for 2-spin systems.
By the SAW tree construction and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we may restrict the graphs to trees.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Before we dig into the general 2-spin system, we first consider a simple case, the hard-core model, the partition function of which is the independence polynomial. This model is the 2-spin system where <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.</annotation></semantics></math> For the hard-core model, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reg23</a>]</cite> proved that LDC holds by using a tool called cluster expansion from statistic physics.
Here, we show that it can also be proved by the following Christoffel-Darboux type identity by Gutman <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gut91</a>]</cite>.
For a graph <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> and a subset <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the graph obtained from <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting all vertices in <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and their adjacent edges (i.e., the subgraph of <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the vertex set <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 21</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> be a tree and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> be two distinct vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for the partition function of the hard-core model on <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{T}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{u,v\}}(\lambda)-Z_{T\setminus\{u\}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{v\}}(\lambda)=-(-\lambda)^{d(u,v)+1}Z_{T\setminus p_{uv}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus N[p_{uv}]}(\lambda)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{T}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{u,v\}}(\lambda)-Z_{T\setminus\{u\}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus\{v\}}(\lambda)=-(-\lambda)^{d(u,v)+1}Z_{T\setminus p_{uv}}(\lambda)Z_{T\setminus N[p_{uv}]}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem21.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem21.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique path connecting <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N[p_{uv}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N[p_{uv}]</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of neighbors of points in <math id="Thmtheorem21.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This identity was extended to general graphs in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ben18</a>]</cite> (Theorem 1.3).
By the SAW tree construction and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>,
the identity for trees is already enough for our proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 22</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the hard-core model defined on a family <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> of graphs closed under taking subgraphs, if the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-free on a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it satisfies point-to-point LDC on <math id="Thmtheorem22.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The case <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(u,v)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(u,v)=1</annotation></semantics></math> is easy to check. Here, we assume that <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(u,v)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(u,v)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For the hard-core model, <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{+}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[v]}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{+}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[v]}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{-}_{G,v}(\lambda)=Z_{G\backslash v}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{-}_{G,v}(\lambda)=Z_{G\backslash v}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{u^{-}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{-,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{-}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{Z^{+}_{G\backslash\{u\},v}}{Z_{G\backslash\{u\}}}=P_{G\backslash\{u\},v}(\lambda)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{u^{-}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{-,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{-}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{Z^{+}_{G\backslash\{u\},v}}{Z_{G\backslash\{u\}}}=P_{G\backslash\{u\},v}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{u^{+}}_{G,v}(\lambda)=\frac{Z^{+,+}_{G,u,v}(\lambda)}{Z^{+}_{G,u}(\lambda)}=\frac{\lambda Z^{+}_{G\backslash N[u],v}}{\lambda Z_{G\backslash N[u]}}=P_{G\backslash N[u],v}(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">