<p id="S3.SS3.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(u,v_{0})=k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(u,v_{0})=k-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we can apply the induction hypothesis, which will finish the induction proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, we argue by induction on <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=d(u,V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda)+d(v,V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda)\geq 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=d(u,V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda)+d(v,V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda)\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math> The the basic case <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2</annotation></semantics></math> is easy to check and the proof of the inductive step is same as the above.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
