<p id="S3.SS3.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> analytic near <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the coefficients of the term <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq d_{G}(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq d_{G}(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> in the Taylor series of <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are equal.
Similar result holds for <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
