<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Zero-freeness implies SSM for <math id="S4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem28" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 28</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem28.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem28.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, a neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system (defined on <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> specified with the fixed parameters <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and a variable <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in U</annotation></semantics></math>) is said to satisfy LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> if for
any <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,
any feasible configurations <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any vertex <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the functions <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and their corresponding Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}(\beta-1/\gamma)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}(\beta-1/\gamma)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}(\beta-1/\gamma)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}(\beta-1/\gamma)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem28.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One can also define point-to-point LDC for <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> similar to the definition of point-to-point LDC for <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem19" title="Definition 19 (Point-to-point LDC). ‣ 3.3 Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>). Similarly, one can prove the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 29</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem29.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If a 2-spin system satisfies point-to-point LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, then it also satisfies LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem29.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 30</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a family of graphs and <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be a complex neighbourhood of <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> such that the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\gamma,\lambda}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\gamma,\lambda}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-free on <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the corresponding 2-spin system satisfies LDC for <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to prove that the system satisfies point-to-point LDC for <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the SAW tree construction and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we only need to consider the case that <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a tree.
Then by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Theorem 23 (Theorem restated). ‣ 3.3 Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

