<p id="S5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of <math id="S5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(+,+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(+,+)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-,-)</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="S5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> under the configuration <math id="S5.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> together with <math id="S5.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> pinned to <math id="S5.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of <math id="S5.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(+,+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(+,+)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-,-)</annotation></semantics></math> edges in <math id="S5.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> under the configuration <math id="S5.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="S5.p10.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m(\sigma)=m^{\prime}(\sigma)+|\{w\in N(v)\mid\sigma(w)=+\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\sigma)=m^{\prime}(\sigma)+|\{w\in N(v)\mid\sigma(w)=+\}|</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of neighbors of <math id="S5.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have</span></p>
