<p id="S5.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G\backslash\{v\}}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{v^{+}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G\backslash\{v\}}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{v^{+}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function of the Ising model with non-uniform external fields <math id="S5.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{v^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{v^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the graph <math id="S5.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from <math id="S5.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting <math id="S5.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{v^{+}}_{w}=\lambda_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{v^{+}}_{w}=\lambda_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V\backslash(N(v)\cup\{v\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V\backslash(N(v)\cup\{v\})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{v^{+}}_{w}=\beta\lambda_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{v^{+}}_{w}=\beta\lambda_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.p10.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in N(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, we have</span></p>
