<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for the partition function <math id="S5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\boldsymbol{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> of the Ising model on a graph <math id="S5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> conditioning on a partial configuration <math id="S5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can delete all vertices in <math id="S5.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, and for every <math id="S5.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V\backslash\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V\backslash\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> multiply the external field <math id="S5.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{n_{+}(w)-n_{-}(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{n_{+}(w)-n_{-}(w)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{+}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{+}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of neighbors of <math id="S5.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> that are pinned to <math id="S5.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S5.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{-}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{-}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of neighbors of <math id="S5.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> that are pinned to <math id="S5.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S5.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We denote <math id="S5.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{n_{+}(w)-n_{-}(w)}\lambda_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{n_{+}(w)-n_{-}(w)}\lambda_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{w}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{w}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p11.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{w}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}})_{w\in V\backslash\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{w}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}})_{w\in V\backslash\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.p11.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
